      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, very clean. \n\nNow, we also want to implement some \"adaptive\" communication. We've noticed that when we use that super formal tone with certain demographics—specifically customers in more urban, inner-city areas or younger, more street-level demographics—it can actually feel a bit cold or even condescending to them. It creates a barrier.\n\nCan you draft a second version of that same delay notification? This one should be much more casual and \"urban-friendly\" so it feels more relatable and builds better rapport with those specific groups. Just make it sound more \"real\" and less corporate.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
